whichever:
Flung back her penny, kicked their fruit
Along whichever road they took,
Not leaving root or stone or shoot;

whips:
Some to work on roads, canals; some to man his ships;
Some to smart in mines beneath sharp overseers' whips;
Some to trap fur-beasts in lands where utmost winter nips.

whirling:
But you danced on, and when some star would spill
Its red and white upon you whirling there,
I sensed a hidden beauty in the air;

Scholars at your study; hunters
Lost amid the whirling winter's
Whiteness uniform;

whisper:
A murmur and a movement drew around;
A naked whisper touched us. Something wrong!
What’s wrong? The black crowd, as an overstrained

whisky:
rotting women at Lagos; the desolation of the Congo; Johnny Walker,
and the millions of whisky bottles buried in the sea along the West
Coast; the daily fights on board, officers, sailors, everybody drunk;

whir:
You Hour! From me you ever take your flight,
Your swift wings wound me as they whir along;
Without you void would be my day and night,

whining:
Across the heavens panted.
"Oh, whining fools," he cried, "have done;
Your wishes shall be granted!"

whilst:
Attempts t' extract the crime-avenging rod,
But, whilst he strives the will of fate t' avert,
Divine Apollo sends a second dart;

I wear the brand of shame;
Whilst he amid the gay and proud
Still bears an honored name.

whirr:
For miles and miles around;
With a wheel and a whirr the resistless rhythm
Trembled incessantly;

whitening:
But here she paused; our eyes had met,
And I was whitening with the jeer;
She rose: 'I went too far,' she said;

whistlin:
An' I 's been 'roun' lots of othahs dat could keep de banjo ringin';
But of all de whistlin' da'kies dat have lived an' died since Ham,
De whistlin'est I evah seed was ol' Ike Bates's Sam.

whippo'will:
Shinin' sof an' white,
Whippo'will a-tellin' tales
Out thaih in de night;

whispah:
An' dey walked an' p'omenaded 'roun' an' thoo an' thoo;
Jealous ol' Mis' Fox, she whispah, "See Mis' Wildcat daih,
Ain't hit scan'lous, huh a-comin' wid huh shouldahs baih?"

whisp'rin:
But I listened kin' o' keerless, not a-t'inkin' 'bout it all;
An' on Sunday, too, I noticed, dey was whisp'rin' mighty much,
Stan'in' all erroun' de roadside w'en dey let us out o' chu'ch.

whimpah:
Set down at dat table thaih;
Jes' you whimpah ef you daih!
Evah mo'nin' on dis place,

whitest:
glow of ice-gentian,
whitest violet;
snow craters

whisking:
Once discerning even one goblin
Racing, whisking, tumbling, hobbling;
Let alone the herds

whizzle:
spider’s lace;
And come the Fall, the whizzle and race
Of the dry, dead leaves when the wind gies chase;
